doc:sch-1-sec-35 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35 Application of amendment" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The amendment of clause 11 of Schedule 1 to the Privacy Act 1988 made by this Part applies in relation to information held after the commencement of this Part, regardless of whether the information was acquired or created before or after that commencement.  Privacy reforms  Schedule 1 Overseas data flows  Part 6 No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2024-sch-1-sec-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36 After subsection 100(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-36 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: (1A) Before the Governor-General makes regulations for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 8.3 prescribing a country or binding scheme, the Minister must be satisfied that: (a) the laws of the country, or the binding scheme, has the effect of protecting personal information about an individual in a way that, overall, is at least substantially similar to the way in which the Australian Privacy Principles protect the information; and (b) there are mechanisms that the individual can access to take action to enforce that protection. (1B) The regulations may prescribe a country or binding scheme for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 8.3 subject to: (a) conditions in relation to a specified entity or class of entities; and (b) conditions in relation to a specified kind or kinds of personal information." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: (1A) Before the Governor-General makes regulations for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 8.3 prescribing a country or binding scheme, the Minister must be satisfied that: (a) the laws of the country, or the binding scheme, has the effect of protecting personal information about an individual in a way that, overall, is at least substantially similar to the way in which the Australian Privacy Principles protect the information; and (b) there are mechanisms that the individual can access to take action to enforce that protection. (1B) The regulations may prescribe a country or binding scheme for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 8.3 subject to: (a) conditions in relation to a specified entity or class of entities; and (b) conditions in relation to a specified kind or kinds of personal information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
