 officer or employee is authorised by the agency to collect, use or disclose the personal information. (6) In this section: designated secrecy provision means any of the following: (a) sections 18, 18A, 18B, 34GF, 35P, 92 and 92A, and subsection 34GE(4), of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979; (b) section 15LC of the Crimes Act 1914; (c) section 34 of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986; (d) sections 39, 40C, 40D and 41 of, and clause 9 of Schedule 1 to, the Intelligence Services Act 2001; (e) sections 42 and 44 of the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018; (f) sections 22, 22A and 22B of the Witness Protection Act 1994;  Schedule 1  Privacy reforms" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

