doc:sch-1-sec-33j-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "33J(5) Reporting on public inquiries" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The Minister must table a copy of the report before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on which the Minister receives the report." ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2024-sch-1-sec-33j-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "33J(6) Reporting on public inquiries"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-33j-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Unless the Minister otherwise directs, the Commissioner must make the report publicly available. Note: The Commissioner may, under section 33B, publish other information relating to the inquiry if it is in the public interest to do so.  Privacy reforms  Schedule 1 Commissioner to conduct public inquiries  Part 10 No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Unless the Minister otherwise directs, the Commissioner must make the report publicly available. Note: The Commissioner may, under section 33B, publish other information relating to the inquiry if it is in the public interest to do so.  Privacy reforms  Schedule 1 Commissioner to conduct public inquiries  Part 10 No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024"@en ;
