doc:sch-2-sec-1-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1 Objects of this Schedule" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The objects of this Schedule are to: (a) establish a cause of action for serious invasions of privacy; and (b) provide for defences, remedies and exemptions in respect of the cause of action; and  Schedule 2  Serious invasions of privacy  Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024 No. 128, 2024 (c) recognise that there is a public interest in protecting privacy; and (d) recognise that the public interest in protecting privacy is balanced with other public interests; and (e) implement Australia’s international obligations in relation to privacy." ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2024-sch-2-sec-2-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 Simplified outline of this Schedule"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-2-2 ;
    values:originalText "This Schedule establishes a cause of action in tort for serious invasions of privacy. An individual has a cause of action against another person if, among other things, the other person invaded the individual’s privacy by intruding upon their seclusion or misusing information relating to them. It is a defence to the cause of action if the other person acted with lawful authority or in certain circumstances involving consent, necessity or the defence of persons or property. If the invasion of privacy involved the publication of information, the other person may also have access to certain defences that would ordinarily arise in the context of defamation proceedings. Exemptions apply in relation to intelligence agencies and law enforcement bodies, persons disclosing information to such agencies or bodies, persons using information disclosed by such agencies or bodies, and persons under 18 years of age. Journalists and certain other persons are also exempt in certain circumstances. The court may, during the proceedings, grant an injunction restraining the other person from invading the individual’s privacy. The court may also summarily dismiss the proceedings in certain circumstances. The court may grant remedies including damages. There are time limits on when proceedings under this Schedule may be commenced.  Serious invasions of privacy  Schedule 2  No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024 This Schedule is intended to be read and construed separately from the rest of this Act." ;
    skos:definition "This Schedule establishes a cause of action in tort for serious invasions of privacy. An individual has a cause of action against another person if, among other things, the other person invaded the individual’s privacy by intruding upon their seclusion or misusing information relating to them. It is a defence to the cause of action if the other person acted with lawful authority or in certain circumstances involving consent, necessity or the defence of persons or property. If the invasion of privacy involved the publication of information, the other person may also have access to certain defences that would ordinarily arise in the context of defamation proceedings. Exemptions apply in relation to intelligence agencies and law enforcement bodies, persons disclosing information to such agencies or bodies, persons using information disclosed by such agencies or bodies, and persons under 18 years of age. Journalists and certain other persons are also exempt in certain circumstances. The court may, during the proceedings, grant an injunction restraining the other person from invading the individual’s privacy. The court may also summarily dismiss the proceedings in certain circumstances. The court may grant remedies including damages. There are time limits on when proceedings under this Schedule may be commenced.  Serious invasions of privacy  Schedule 2  No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024 This Schedule is intended to be read and construed separately from the rest of this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f8edeee620d66503414d2a840605a905295218f4de7012ca713dd129af60d059" ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Establishes a cause of action in tort for serious invasions of privacy." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
