concept:privacy-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2024-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7(6) Cause of action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Without limiting the matters that the court may consider in determining whether the invasion of privacy was serious, the court may consider the following:  Serious invasions of privacy  Schedule 2  No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (a) the degree of any offence, distress or harm to dignity that the invasion of privacy was likely to cause to a person of ordinary sensibilities in the position of the plaintiff; (b) whether the defendant knew or ought to have known that the invasion of privacy was likely to offend, distress or harm the dignity of the plaintiff; (c) if the invasion of privacy was intentional—whether the defendant was motivated by malice. Untrue information" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Without limiting the matters that the court may consider in determining whether the invasion of privacy was serious, the court may consider the following:  Serious invasions of privacy  Schedule 2  No. 128, 2024 Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (a) the degree of any offence, distress or harm to dignity that the invasion of privacy was likely to cause to a person of ordinary sensibilities in the position of the plaintiff; (b) whether the defendant knew or ought to have known that the invasion of privacy was likely to offend, distress or harm the dignity of the plaintiff; (c) if the invasion of privacy was intentional—whether the defendant was motivated by malice. Untrue information"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e7a9bf81fb73e85bb0f5792693d3753c9496609278752d45a20542e86976e86d" ;
